## `-setup-be` Backend Scaffold Flow

**Agent:** `backend-engineer`

Ask all at once:
1. Target root path? (default: `backend/`)
2. First module name? (default: `example`)
3. Create stub `pyproject.toml` + `run.py`? (yes/no)

Create this tree:
```
<backend_root>/
├── run.py
├── pyproject.toml
├── migrations/
├── seeders/
├── scripts/
├── tests/
├── docs/
└── app/
    ├── app.py
    ├── config/
    │   ├── settings.py
    │   └── database.py
    ├── utils/
    └── modules/
        └── <module_name>/
            ├── __init__.py
            ├── routes/routes.py
            ├── controllers/controller.py
            ├── services/
            │   ├── create_*.py
            │   ├── get_*.py
            │   ├── update_*.py
            │   └── delete_*.py
            ├── helpers/
            ├── models/
            │   ├── request_models.py
            │   ├── response_models.py
            │   └── db_models.py
            └── tests/
                └── test_<module_name>.py
```

Call chain: `app.py → routes → controllers → services → models` (helpers shared)

Wire module into `app.py`:
```python
from app.modules.<module>.routes.routes import router as <module>_router
app.include_router(<module>_router)
```

